Guided Exercise: Reproducible Deployments with OpenShift Image Streams
Objective
Deploy an application using image streams to reference container images indirectly, ensuring reproducible deployments.
Outcomes:
•	Create an image stream and image stream tag.
•	Deploy an application using the image stream tag.
•	Confirm deployment uses the SHA ID of the container image.
________________________________________
Step 1: Prepare the Lab
lab start updates-imagestreams
•	Sets up resources for the exercise.
•	Creates updates-imagestreams project.
•	Generates resources.txt with image names and commands.
________________________________________
Step 2: Log in to OpenShift
oc login -u developer -p developer https://api.ocp4.example.com:6443
oc project updates-imagestreams
•	Logs in as developer.
•	Sets the active project to updates-imagestreams.
________________________________________
Step 3: Create Image Stream
oc create is versioned-hello
•	Creates an image stream named versioned-hello.
________________________________________
Step 4: Create Image Stream Tag
oc tag registry.ocp4.example.com:8443/redhattraining/versioned-hello:v1.0 versioned-hello:v1.0
•	Creates the v1.0 tag in versioned-hello pointing to the source image.
•	Ensures the tag references the image by SHA ID.
________________________________________
Step 5: Enable Image Stream Lookup
oc set image-lookup versioned-hello
oc set image-lookup
•	Enables local lookup so Kubernetes workloads in the project can reference the image stream by short name.
•	Verification:
NAME             LOCAL
versioned-hello  true
________________________________________
Step 6: Verify SHA ID
oc describe is versioned-hello
oc image info registry.ocp4.example.com:8443/redhattraining/versioned-hello:v1.0 | head
•	Confirms the image stream tag references the SHA ID of the source image.
•	Ensures deployment consistency even if the registry image is updated later.
________________________________________
Step 7: Create Deployment Using Image Stream Tag
oc create deployment version --image versioned-hello:v1.0
•	Deployment references image stream tag instead of a direct registry image.
________________________________________
Step 8: Verify Pod and Deployment
oc get pods
oc get deployment -o wide
oc get pod <pod-name> -o jsonpath='{.spec.containers[0].image}{"\n"}'
•	Confirms that both deployment and pod use the SHA ID of the image.
•	Ensures reproducible deployment.
________________________________________
Step 9: Finish Lab
lab finish updates-imagestreams
•	Cleans up resources.
•	Prevents interference with subsequent exercises.
________________________________________
✅ Key Takeaways
1.	Image streams decouple deployments from registry image names.
2.	SHA IDs ensure reproducibility of deployments.
3.	Image stream lookup allows short names in deployments.
4.	Image streams enable controlled updates and rollbacks.

